  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION Purchasers\nof common shares in this offering will experience immediate and substantial dilution to the extent of the difference between the\ninitial public offering price per common share paid by the purchasers of the common shares in this offering and the pro\nforma, as adjusted net tangible book value per common share immediately after, and giving effect to, this offering. Dilution results\nfrom the fact that the initial public offering price per common share in this offering is substantially in excess of the net tangible\nbook value per common share attributable to the issued and outstanding common shares held by our existing shareholders. Our historical net tangible\nbook value per common share is determined by dividing our net tangible book value, which is the book value of our total assets less the\nbook value of our goodwill, intangible assets, deferred initial public offering ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
